    <Container width="content" class="mt-16">
      <div class="case-layout-cont">
        <div class="measure space-y-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted text-lg">
          <p>
            Underneath both, attendance isn't stored as a separate on-or-off flag. It's
            worked out fresh each time from the full history of check-ins and
            check-outs. That takes more computing work, but it buys correctness: a
            saved flag can drift out of sync the moment any of the several ways to log
            a check, by voice, on the tablet, on the board, or through the connected
            systems, forgets to update it. The same reasoning produced the rule that
            enrollment status is worked out from start and end dates and never manually
            switched, so a provider can never leave a child marked active six months
            after they left. A wrong headcount is a licensing problem, not a display bug.
          </p>
