  <Section tone="ink" padding="loose">
    <Container width="wide">
      <p class="mono-label !text-paper/65 mb-6">Product design engineering</p>
      <Heading level={2} visual="display-lg" tone="paper" class="max-w-3xl">
        Some decisions don&rsquo;t survive a spec boundary.
      </Heading>
      <Text size="lg" tone="whiteMuted" class="mt-5 max-w-2xl">
        &ldquo;Failure is expected, not exceptional&rdquo; is a screen, a queue, a status
        field, two flags marking why something failed, and a saved audio recording.
        &ldquo;Names are the hard part&rdquo; is a form field, an automated background
        task, a pattern-matching rule, and a set of clickable word chips writing back
        into that same list. Those only work when the person drawing the screen and the
        person deciding what the recognition system returns are the same person. If
        that&rsquo;s the bar you&rsquo;re hiring for, let&rsquo;s talk.
      </Text>
